cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PyStatlas, please cite it as below."
title: "PyStatlas: A Python Gallery of Statistical Graphics for the Social Sciences"
abstract: "An open-source gallery of statistical charts for Python, written first for social-science students. Charts are organised by the question they answer; nearly every example is set in one of the author's published papers (or in the CIRANO GVCdtLab digital twin of the Great Lakes–St. Lawrence corridor) and runs on a small, labelled simulation, not the papers' data. Every figure reports the statistics behind it (estimates, confidence intervals, tests, effect sizes) and comes with a short, self-contained script."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Warin
    given-names: Thierry
    website: "https://www.warin.ca"
repository-code: "https://github.com/warint/pystatlas"
url: "https://warint.github.io/pystatlas/"
license: MIT
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-08"
keywords:
